  "DiscoveryIsAuthoritative": false,
  "DiscoveryIsAuthoritativeRationale": "Set to FALSE (the conservative/safe default) despite one CANDIDATE endpoint worth flagging for a future iteration: every Vanilla community serves its own live OpenAPI v3 document at `{communityUrl}/api/v2/openapi/v3` (this build''s own two source specs were fetched from exactly this endpoint on two different communities -- see SOURCES.json), and it IS permission-gated on at least one tested community (success.vanillaforums.com returns HTTP 403 ''Garden.Settings.Manage'' for anonymous requests; open.vanillaforums.com serves it unauthenticated). The two communities'' specs also differ in size (237 vs. 316 paths) in a way CONSISTENT with per-community addon-scoping. However, this build could NOT confirm (credential-free) whether that size difference reflects (a) a genuinely per-tenant, permission-scoped, complete-gamut catalog of what THIS credential can access, or (b) merely a different installed product/addon build being served identically to every caller regardless of the caller''s own permissions -- both are consistent with the observed evidence, and connector-code-conventions.md requires EVIDENCE the endpoint ''enumerates the COMPLETE gamut the credentials expose'' before flipping this flag, not a plausible hypothesis. No CODE PATH in this connector build (Declared-metadata-only, no live DiscoverObjects/DiscoverFields implementation yet) calls this endpoint, so there is also no implementation evidence to point to. Recorded here as a CANDIDATE for CodeBuild/a future iteration to empirically resolve via a live-credentialed probe (does the SAME community''s /openapi/v3 response change when queried with tokens from users holding different permission sets, and does it omit an addon-disabled door only in the way the addon actually differs?) -- until then, DiscoveryIsAuthoritative stays FALSE per the safe default: per-tenant addon variance (Knowledge Base, Webhooks, AI settings, third-party integration configs, custom Profile Fields) means any given customer community exposes a DIFFERENT subset of the 51 coverable objects than another (e.g. a community without the Knowledge Base addon will 404 on /knowledge-bases), and the BaseRESTIntegrationConnector default (cache-driven IntrospectSchema re-reading persisted ACTIVE metadata, itself non-authoritative) applies. Runtime DiscoverObjects/DiscoverFields for this connector, if implemented against a live community, would today be SCOPED to that tenant''s actually-enabled addons -- so absence of an object on a comprehensive refresh must NOT deactivate it (it may simply be an addon this tenant hasn''t enabled, or the tenant''s token lacks the permission to see it), per connector-code-conventions.md''s authoritative-discovery + deactivation rule. Custom (admin-configured) Profile Fields ARE fully runtime-discoverable via the `/profile-fields` door and flow through ordinary Discovered-metadata + the framework''s custom-column capture, independent of this authoritative-discovery decision.",
  "OutOfScopeObjectFamilies": [],
  "OutOfScopeObjectFamiliesRationale": "No out-of-scope product family was identified by SourceAudit (SOURCE_STUDY.md §8 scopeDecision: ''none identified''). Both credential-free source communities probed (open.vanillaforums.com and success.vanillaforums.com) are live instances of the SAME single, unified Vanilla API v2 contract -- they simply have different ADDON subsets enabled (Knowledge Base/Articles/Analytics/AI-settings on success.vanillaforums.com only; a broader core forum/discussion feature set with no Knowledge Base on open.vanillaforums.com) rather than being separate product lines, so the merged 335-path/380-schema/51-coverable-object union is treated as ONE in-scope surface, not partitioned into in-scope vs out-of-scope families. The SSO/OAuth2/SAML/OIDC/jsConnect authentication FLOWS are deliberately NOT modeled as an ''out-of-scope object family'' either -- they have no independently-addressable REST CRUD surface in API v2 at all (they are Dashboard-configured authentication infrastructure, not syncable record types), so they are recorded instead as end-user auth awareness (see EndUserSSOMechanisms) rather than as a scoped-out object family. If a future connector iteration needs SSO CONFIGURATION itself as syncable data, a dedicated follow-up source pass would be needed (no such REST surface was found in this build''s evidence trail).",
  "PerTenantAddonVarianceNote": "Per SOURCE_STUDY.md §8: any given customer Vanilla community may have a DIFFERENT subset of the 51 coverable objects actually enabled depending on which addons that community has turned on (Knowledge Base/Articles, Webhooks, AI settings/processing, third-party integration configs such as Jira/Salesforce/Sprinklr/Hootsuite are all addon-gated). This is normal, expected SaaS-addon variance, not a source-coverage gap -- the Declared metadata seeded from this build''s research represents the FULL possible surface across all addons; per-tenant absence of a given addon''s objects is handled by runtime discovery / graceful 404 handling at connection time, not by narrowing the Declared catalog itself.",
  "ReactionEventScopeNote": "CORRECTED (amendment): reaction-EVENT endpoints DO exist and are now emitted as the DiscussionReaction (/discussions/{id}/reactions) and CommentReaction (/comments/{id}/reactions) IOs — each a paginated GET (page/limit) + POST (react) + DELETE .../{userID} (un-react) returning individual reaction events (recordType, recordID, userID, tagID, dateInserted). These are DISTINCT from ReactionType (/reactions), which is the catalog of possible reaction kinds keyed by urlCode. The prior note incorrectly asserted these event endpoints were absent from the merged spec; that was falsifiable against sources/vanilla-openapi.merged.v3.json and is superseded."
}' EXEC [__mj].spCreateIntegration @Name = @Name_89f1f3d1,
  @Description = @Description_89f1f3d1,
  @NavigationBaseURL = @NavigationBaseURL_89f1f3d1,
  @ClassName = @ClassName_89f1f3d1,
  @ImportPath = @ImportPath_89f1f3d1,
  @BatchMaxRequestCount = @BatchMaxRequestCount_89f1f3d1,
  @BatchRequestWaitTime = @BatchRequestWaitTime_89f1f3d1,
  @ID = @ID_89f1f3d1,
  @CredentialTypeID = @CredentialTypeID_89f1f3d1,
  @Icon = @Icon_89f1f3d1,
  @Configuration = @Configuration_89f1f3d1;

GO

